            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0698" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.232/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-17T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>43. Embassy’s telegram number 42 of September 12.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d604-f1"
                    /> Received note from Foreign Office today which states that the Government of
                    Peru is willing to negotiate treaty as soon as possible. The note adds that Peru
                    desires that in the proposed treaty we grant to Peruvian sugar the same
                    treatment which is now conceded to Cuban sugar. Will the Department please
                    telegraph me its views for my confidential information and guidance before
                    negotiations start? Texts of notes exchanged will go forward in next
                        pouch.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d604-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
